<style>
    :root {
        /* Primary Colors */
        --colour-text: #495057;
        /* TEXT  */
        @@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&display=swap');

        .header-container,
        .card,
        .bottom-container,
        .abt, 
        .bottom-card,
        .blood-list {
            color: var(--colour-text);
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        }

        /* UPPER PAGE CONTENTS */
        .header-container {
            padding: 40px 20px;
            margin: 2rem auto;
            max-width: 1100px;
            width: 100%;
        }

        .Header1 {
            font-family: sans-serif;
            font-weight: 700;
            font-size: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        }

        .DonationP {
            font-weight: 400;
            letter-spacing: 0.5px;
            font-family: sans-serif;
            font-size: 15px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            max-width: 65ch;
        }
        /* CAROUSEL */
        .Carouselcontainer {
            margin: 3rem auto 2rem auto;
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 1100px;
            padding: 0 1rem;
        }

        .carousel-inner img {
            width: 100%;
            height: 350px;
            object-fit: cover;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }
        /* CARDS */
        .CardsContainer {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            margin-top: 3rem;
            padding: 20px 10px 50px;
            gap: 20px;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
        }

        .card {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            background-color: #ffffff;
            padding: 50px 25px;
            flex: 1;
            border-radius: 12px;
            border: 1px solid #cccccc;
            width: 400px;
            height: 350px;
            aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
        }

            .card h1 {
                font-size: 1.4rem;
                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
            }

            .card p, .card li {
                line-height: 1.4;
                font-size: 0.85rem;
            }

            .card ul {
                padding-left: 1.2rem;
                margin: 0;
            }
        /* BOTTOM SECTION */
        .abt {
            margin-top: 3rem;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .bottom-container {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: flex-start;
            margin: 5rem auto 4rem auto;
            max-width: 1100px;
            padding: 0 1rem;
            gap: 2rem;
        }

        .columntext {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 2rem;
            flex: 1;
        }

        .about {
            max-width: 50ch;
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .card.bottom-card {
            max-width: 45ch;
            width: 100%;
            flex-shrink: 0;
            height: auto;
            min-height: 20rem;
        }

        .blood-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding: 0;
            margin: 0;
        }

            .blood-list li {
                padding: 8px 0;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
                font-size: 0.9rem;
            }
</style>

@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}



        <div class="header-container">
            <div>
                <h1 class="Header1">Donations save lives.</h1>
            </div>

            <div>
                <p class="DonationP">
                    Every drop of blood goes towards someone in need.
                    Blood cannot be synthetically made, and patients rely
                    entirely on donors for everything ranging from surgeries
                    to blood disorders. By donating, you provide doctors to
                    help patients and individuals a second chance at life.
                    A single donation takes less than an hour but can save up
                    to three lives!
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>


        <div class="Carouselcontainer">
            <div id="carouselExampleAutoplaying" class="carousel slide" data-bs-ride="carousel">
                <div class="carousel-inner">
                    <div class="carousel-item active" data-bs-interval="4000">
                <img src="~/Images/BloodDonation1.png" class="d-block w-100" alt="N1">
                    </div>
                    <div class="carousel-item" data-bs-interval="4000">
                        <img src="~/Images/BloodDonation2.jpg" class="d-block w-100" alt="N2">
                    </div>
                    <div class="carousel-item" data-bs-interval="4000">
                        <img src="~/Images/BloodDonation3.jpg" class="d-block w-100" alt="N3">
                    </div>
                    <div class="carousel-item" data-bs-interval="4000">
                        <img src="~/Images/BloodDonation4.jpg" class="d-block w-100" alt="N4">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <button class="carousel-control-prev" type="button" data-bs-target="#carouselExampleAutoplaying" data-bs-slide="prev">
                    <span class="carousel-control-prev-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden">Previous</span>
                </button>
                <button class="carousel-control-next" type="button" data-bs-target="#carouselExampleAutoplaying" data-bs-slide="next">
                    <span class="carousel-control-next-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden">Next</span>
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="CardsContainer">
            <div class="card">
                <h1>Preparation</h1>
                <p>
                    Please bring a valid form of ID and fill out a Donor details form.
                    Completing the form ensures your health information is complete and
                    you consent to testing.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h1>Health Assessment</h1>
                <p>
                    After you've completed the form, a finger prick test will be needed in
                    order to check your haemoglobin level. This is a confidential process
                    and no one may  accompany you except children under the age of 5. This
                    is to ensure the interview will be done in a consistent manner and free
                    from any external influence.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h1>Eligibility Criteria</h1>
                <ul>
                    <li>New donors can donate blood between the ages 16 and 71</li>
                    <li>Existing donors can donate until 75 and may continue until 81 with consent from a NZBS Medical Officer</li>
                    <li>You must weigh 50 kg or more and be atleast 150 cm tall</li>
                    <li>You must be in good health at the time you donate</li>
                    <li>You must wait 3 months if you've recently had a tattoo (including cosmetic tattoos)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="abt">
            <h1>All blood types can donate blood!</h1>
        </div>

        <div class="bottom-container">

            <div class="columntext">
                <div class="about">
                    <p>
                        Anybody can donate blood, with O
                        negative being the only bloodtype
                        that can be safely given to anybody!
                        This is because O negative have no antigens
                        in their blood red cells, causing no reaction
                        in other peoples immune system. This makes it
                        essential for emergency situations.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="about">
                    <p>
                        Approximately 6% to 8% of the world's population has
                        O-negative (O-) blood making it quite rare compared
                        to other blood types making up 13% of hospital blood requests.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card bottom-card">
                <div>
                    <h1>BLOOD TYPES</h1>
                    <ul class="blood-list">
                        <li>A Positive (A+)</li>
                        <li>A Negative (A-)</li>
                        <li>B Positive (B+)</li>
                        <li>B Negative (B-)</li>
                        <li>AB Positive (AB+)</li>
                        <li>AB Negative (AB-)</li>
                        <li>O Positive (O+)</li>
                        <li>O Negative (O-)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
